{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"GROUNDING (plan-review E4/T8): the plan conflated TWO distinct multi-attempt mechanisms. Verified in code (worktree at S3 tip):\n\nMECHANISM A — FallbackModel candidates (model_classes.build_fallback_model, model_classes.py:414-434): builds FallbackModel(*models), candidates with N+1 concrete models (primary first). FallbackModel iterates candidates WITHIN ONE agent.run; pydantic-ai counts ONE model-request/turn. These are the candidate CHILD spans under one logical Agent-request span (AC-1, AC-2).\n\nMECHANISM B — native->prompted downgrade (structured_run._pai_structured, structured_run.py:118-145): calls _run_native_output (agent.run_sync #1, structured_run.py:210) and, on a 895c grammar-compilation rejection, _run_prompted_output (agent.run_sync #2, structured_run.py:248). This is TWO SEPARATE Agent runs => TWO Agent-request spans (native attempt RAISED, prompted attempt RETURNED), a distinct orchestration-layer mechanism — NOT a FallbackModel candidate, and it DOES add a second Agent request by design. Each of those two runs may itself contain Mechanism-A candidate child spans.\n\nConsequence: AC-3 must stop claiming 'candidate outcomes without adding an Agent request' and instead verify two distinct logical-turn spans from the downgrade, instrumented at the _pai_structured boundary (Scope must add structured_run.py).\n\nAlso grounded: pydantic-ai 1.107.2 exposes NO public InstrumentedModel; the Agent model-request span is pydantic_ai._instrumentation.open_model_request_span (active under setup_tracing/Agent.instrument_all). S4 candidate spans nest beneath it via the ambient OTel span context and reuse runner.py provenance (provider_provenance['candidates'], runner.py:458-463). tracing.py today only exposes setup_tracing() (OTel TracerProvider + instrument_all), lazy-imported => lean-import safe. No in-memory-exporter test exists yet; a new test uses opentelemetry InMemorySpanExporter."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786961883744514001,"uuid":"a8063569-044d-46d0-b644-b314299c364f"}